From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuttlely vendor <vendor@cuttlely.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlely: delegate roster allowlist and synchronous chief
 delegation

What: tools/delegate_tool_toolsets.py reads the profile's harness-roster.json and grants each specialist the toolset allowlist stored there. The chief profile only enables delegation, memory and session_search. tools/delegate_tool.py passes that allowlist to the child instead of inheriting the parent's toolsets, and run_agent.py keeps a Cuttlely harness chief's delegate_task synchronous.

Why: Cuttlely decides which tools each specialist may use, and the chat waits on the chief's turn, so each specialist result has to come back as the tool output in that turn, not in the background.
---
 run_agent.py                    |  8 +++-
 tools/delegate_tool.py          |  6 ++-
 tools/delegate_tool_toolsets.py | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

